  description:
    "The Tarsar Marsar trek takes you to **two of Kashmir's most beautiful alpine lakes**, through meadows and passes above the Aru and Pahalgam valleys. From the green Aru Valley it reaches **the glacially carved bowl of Tarsar at 3,720m**, crosses the pass above it and descends to **the wild, remote Marsar lake** — less visited and arguably more dramatic — with **the Kolahoi glacier glinting in the distance**. The margs and shepherd encampments along the way give an authentic slice of Kashmiri high-altitude life: Kashmir trekking at its finest.",
  whoFor: "You've done a multi-day trek before · You can manage two pass days around 4,000m back to back · 6–7 nights of tent camping beside alpine lakes is what you want · You can go in Jul–Aug, the only reliable window",
  whoNot: "You need phone signal: prepaid SIMs from outside J&K don't work there (postpaid does) · You can only go outside Jul–Aug: snow or closures make the route unreliable · You'd skip registering: the forest checkpost at Aru needs your details and ID",
  safetyNotes:
    "Aru requires Pahalgam-area permits for foreigners. The pass between Tarsar and Marsar is steep and can be snowy in July. Register at the Forest Department checkpost at Aru before starting.",
